{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1551118059,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2NzExNTc4Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3179#issuecomment-467115782"},"message":"I find that section confusing too.\n\n\u003e When doing the next suggested command, \"datalad install ///openfmri/ds000002\" is seems I should have \"cd datalad/openfmri\" first.\n\nI don't think the second command was intended as follow-up to the first, and the first command certainly isn't needed to run the second.  In the second command's description, \"any known dataset can now be installed inside the local superdataset [...]\", \"local superdataset\" would more accurately be \"current directory\".\n\nAnother confusing bit is that this introduces two different flavors of `///`: the [local variant][l] (mentioned in output of the first command) and the [remote variant][r] used in the second install command.\n\n[l]: http://docs.datalad.org/en/latest/basics.html#dataset-argument\n[r]: http://docs.datalad.org/en/latest/basics.html#downloading-datalad-s-default-superdataset","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1551118136,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIxNjI1NjM2MTE="},"added":["documentation"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1551147552,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2NzI2NjAwNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3179#issuecomment-467266006"},"message":"yeah, could be improved.  I guess we could RF that **First steps** to operate on that local clone of `///`, thus adjusting the install command to be `datalad install ~/datalad/openfmri/ds000002`.  And then just adding a remark that in principle every such (sub)dataset is a full featured dataset and could be installed independently into an arbitrary other location (e.g. via `datalad install ///openfmri/ds000002`).\nBut then someone (voices of revolution are in my head!)  could chime in that \"First steps\" is not even about search/install but should be about \"create/add/save\" ;-)\nside-topic:\nOverall docs clearly could be cleaned up and improved. For starters I think the [\"Data management use cases\"](http://docs.datalad.org/en/latest/usecases/index.html#chap-usecases) should be one way or another integrated or replaced by [DataLad Features](https://www.datalad.org/features) from the main webpage","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1568960801,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzMzQyNTI5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3179#issuecomment-533425292"},"message":"This has now been fixed by obliteration ;-)\n\nBetter introductory docs are now available in the handbook at http://handbook.datalad.org and the docs at http://docs.datalad.org will (and do) cover more technical aspects and API.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1568960801,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjY0OTI0MDAyNA=="},"status":2}]}